sourcebody='''The worker01 continuation found source-specific preparation and formula defects that prevent safe ingredient resolution. These observations are separate from the blank-label shared-ID1944 defect in [KG-Microbe #1824](https://github.com/Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe/issues/1824). No source response or maintained dataset was changed.

| Source case | Observed primary-source problem | Required follow-up |
| --- | --- | --- |
| MediaDive ingredient572, DSMZ559/1840/1903 | One compoundID is used for2mL of5%w/v thiosulfate stock,10mL/L of2M aqueous stock, and10g dry reagent. The admitted559 row also reports derived1667g/L and10543.3mmol/L, inconsistent with the stated addition. | Preserve occurrence-specific stock/reagent qualifiers; correct derived quantity at the owning transform/source without replacing raw amount/unit or globally assigning the anhydrous form. |
| MediaDive ingredient2389, DSMZ589 | Admitted recipe says water(distilled or tapwater), but original DSMZ PDF says Distilled water only. | Establish provenance of the tapwater alternative; model a recipe choice or correct the occurrence. It is not a mixture of two waters. |
| MediaDive ingredient804, DSMZ863 | Both API and original PDF printNa2Se2O3,0.100g in trace stock. | Obtain authoritative reagent/formula correction; do not silently redirect toNa2SeO3. |
| MediaDive ingredient870, DSMZ973 | Both API and original PDF printNa2Se3×5H2O,0.50mg. | Obtain authoritative clarification; lexical resemblance is insufficient to assign sodium selenite pentahydrate. |
| DSMZ1783 Solution2 | K2HPO4 amount15.30 has no unit in both API and original PDF. | Obtain the missing unit; no guessedgram assignment. |
| JCM1419 | Primary prints0.1 M M FeCl2 solution. | Preserve literal label and seek authoritative concentration-token correction. |
| JCM1462, inherited1463/1464 Ni/Se/W stock | Primary printsNa2WO2·2H2O,0.4mg/L. | Do not replaceWO2withWO4 from a familiar tungstate name without source correction. |
| DSMZ436 Mineral solution2 / MediaDive solution884 | Primary PDF and API both printCaCl2·7H2O and percentages without a basis. | Clarify calcium hydrate and percent basis before exact quantitative component grounding; this is not merely an API transcription error. |

The explicit numerical/representation conflicts are actionable defects. Unusual source formulas and missing units are precise clarification requirements; this report does not decide what the intended chemistry must have been. Source-scoped preparations with complete formulas remain resolved contexts and are not added to a generic composition-missing backlog.

Evidence and exact case/occurrence bindings: '''+link('root_substances/kg26/findings-and-dedup-plan.json')+', '+link('named_stocks/issues-for-root.json')+', '+link('concentration_stocks/findings-for-root.json')+'''. Preserve original timestamps, hashes, raw labels and source-count definitions. Acceptance requires source/version-bound corrections plus a re-review of affected downstream mappings; a structurally valid export is not chemical approval.
'''
